### Page 1 of 3

```text
1102 WEST 19TH STREET  ●  P.O. BOX 2073  ●  CHEYENNE, WYOMING  82003  ●  307/634-7273

January 16, 2018
TO:
Eric Hammer, Planner I, City of Cheyenne Development Office
CC:
Public Services Committee of the Cheyenne City Council
Robert Briggs, Planning & Development Director
InRe: POSTPONEMENT REQUEST for SWEETGRASS ANNEXATION #UDC-17-00542
Dear Mr. Hammer,
I would like to begin this postponement request by expressing how appreciative we are to yourself,
Development Office staff, and the City Council for your collaboration and patience as this project has
carried into the new year. We understand, both from our own perspective, as well as for your office and
the Governing Body, that it is never desirable to string a project along as long as this one has continued.
As you know, the primary reason for the extraordinary postponement(s) on this particular annexation
request has been to work through the Annexation Agreement for a project of this unique size and scope;
in addition, this annexation has been more complicated than most, not just because of sheer size, but
also due to the unique nature of the proposed PUD and the specific and innovative provisions of the
Agreement - including alternative road sections promoting the unique neighborhood character
envisioned by the owner, and a self-imposed additional “Transportation Impact Fee” to assist in
mitigation of foreseeable traffic impacts.
As noted above, we have been diligently working with City staff to iron out the provisions of the
Agreement and as of today, Tuesday January 16, we believe we have reached consensus between the
City and the Owner(s) on all the provisions and particular language of the agreement. This will enable
the agreement to be submitted to the Council agenda for first reading at the January 22 Regular meeting;
Obviously, in order for the Agreement to be valid to the Annexation, this necessitates one more
postponement of the Annexation Request. It is our hope that any issues or discrepancies that may be
identified as the Agreement moves through Governing Body approval, can be easily remedied and that
both the Agreement and the actual Annexation may be approved by the full Council on February 12.
Again we appreciate your patience and understanding, and Steil Surveying Services, on behalf of the
owner, hereby requests that the above-described Annexation (3rd Reading) be postponed from the
scheduled January 22 City Council meeting (Postpone at January 16 Public Services Committee)
in order to allow for the Annexation Agreement to “catch-up” with the Annexation itself. It is our
understanding that the most recent attached Annexation map, dated 10/20/2017, is accepted and requires
no further revisions. Additionally, for the benefit of the Committee, you will find attached the proposed
1st Filing Preliminary Plat currently under review as UDC-18-00001 and the accompanying proposed
Development Concept.
We anticipate that following this request, the Annexation request will be placed on the Public Services
Committee agenda for February 5, 2018 and, barring any further request for postponement, will be heard
on 3rd & final reading by the full City Council on February 12.
Please contact me with any questions or concerns.
Thank you and best regards,

Casey L. Palma, AICP
Steil Surveying Services, LLC
CPalma@SteilSurvey.com
```

